config K1_SDIO_WIFI_CCCR_ABORT_RESET
	bool "Reset SDIO I/O functions through CCCR_ABORT before enumeration"
	default n
	depends on K1_SDIO_WIFI
	---help---
		Before CMD0/CMD5, read CCCR_ABORT, set its RES bit, and write it back
		to reset stale SDIO I/O-function state inherited across a RAM-only
		handoff.  This mirrors the optional Linux sdio_reset() recovery step.
		It is disabled by default: on the MUSE Pi Pro, a successful RES write
		requires an additional card-recovery sequence before SDR104 tuning can
		be considered usable.  A failed early reset is recorded but does not
		prevent the ordinary enumeration sequence.

